title: The Left Radicals after Kapp
subtitle: Hamburg and Bremen draw their own lessons from March.
new-page: true
tags: event
view-if: year = 1920 and month = 4 and crisis = 0 and ultraleft_gone = 0 and ultraleft_crisis_1920 = 0 and ending_id = 0
max-visits: 1
priority: 3
on-arrival: {!
Q.ultraleft_crisis_1920 = 1;
Q.e20_lead_ul = (Q.leading_faction == 'ultraleft') ? 1 : 0;
Q.e20_lux_in = Q.luxemburgist_gone ? 0 : 1;
// the Left Radicals' weight in the districts, for a congress
Q.e20_ul_power = Q.ultraleft_strength + Q.history_ultraleft * 2 - Q.history_luxemburgist - Q.history_unionist;
!}

= The Left Radicals after Kapp

[? if e20_lead_ul = 0 : The Left Radicals stayed in the party after Heidelberg. Their conference in Hamburg now demands that we leave the "counter-revolutionary" unions, boycott the June election and build factory organisations instead. They have given the Zentrale until the end of the month. ?]

[? if e20_lead_ul = 1 : The Left Radicals hold the Zentrale. They mean to take the party out of the unions and found a General Workers' Union of factory organisations. From Moscow comes a sharp letter: the International expects its German section to work in the unions and in parliament. ?]

- @expel: Expel the Left Radicals.
- @congress: Let a party congress decide.
- @union: Found the General Workers' Union.
- @moscow: Bow to Moscow and go back into the unions.

@expel
subtitle: A second Heidelberg. Their districts will walk out with them.
view-if: e20_lead_ul = 0
on-arrival: {!
Q.e20_split_lost = 0;
for (var d of Q.districts) {
    if (Q['district_' + d + '_faction'] == 'ultraleft') {
        var lost = Q['district_' + d + '_members'] * 0.6;
        Q.e20_split_lost += lost;
        Q['district_' + d + '_members'] -= lost;
        Q['district_' + d + '_faction'] = Q.leading_faction;
        Q['district_' + d + '_loyalty'] = 50;
    }
}
Q.ultraleft_gone = 1;
Q.ultraleft_satisfaction = 0;
Q.kapd_split = 1;
Q.kapd_exists = 1;
Q.kapd_members = Math.round(Q.e20_split_lost + 8);
Q.kapd_relation = 10;
if (Q.junior_faction == 'ultraleft') { Q.junior_faction = 0; }
Q.unity += 12;
Q.e20_split_lost = Q.e20_split_lost.toFixed(1);
Q.lean_luxemburgist += 2;
RG.news('Communist Zentrale expels Hamburg and Bremen', 3);
!}

About [+ e20_split_lost +] thousand members leave with the Hamburg and Bremen leaders. Within days they found the Communist Workers' Party of Germany, the KAPD.

@congress
subtitle: [? if e20_ul_power >= 35 : The districts that fought in March lean their way. ?][? if e20_ul_power < 35 : Most districts are with the Zentrale. ?] Whoever loses will leave.
view-if: e20_lead_ul = 0
on-arrival: {!
Q.e20_ul_won = Q.e20_ul_power + Math.floor(Math.random() * 11) - 5 >= 35 ? 1 : 0;
if (Q.e20_ul_won) {
    Q.junior_faction = Q.leading_faction;
    Q.leading_faction = 'ultraleft';
    Q.election_boycott = 1;
    Q.unity -= 8;
} else {
    Q.e20_split_lost = 0;
    for (var d of Q.districts) {
        if (Q['district_' + d + '_faction'] == 'ultraleft') {
            var lost = Q['district_' + d + '_members'] * 0.5;
            Q.e20_split_lost += lost;
            Q['district_' + d + '_members'] -= lost;
            Q['district_' + d + '_faction'] = Q.leading_faction;
            Q['district_' + d + '_loyalty'] = 55;
        }
    }
    Q.ultraleft_gone = 1;
    Q.ultraleft_satisfaction = 0;
    Q.kapd_split = 1;
    Q.kapd_exists = 1;
    Q.kapd_members = Math.round(Q.e20_split_lost + 6);
    Q.kapd_relation = 15;
    if (Q.junior_faction == 'ultraleft') { Q.junior_faction = 0; }
    Q.unity += 10;
}
!}

[? if e20_ul_won = 1 : The congress meets in Berlin in mid-April. The Left Radicals take the Zentrale, and the party will boycott the election. ?][? if e20_ul_won = 0 : The congress backs the Zentrale. The Left Radical delegates walk out singing the *Internationale* and found the KAPD, with fewer members behind them than they had hoped. ?]

@union
subtitle: The shipyards and some of the pits will follow. Eight million workers will stay in the old unions.
view-if: e20_lead_ul = 1
on-arrival: {!
Q.worker_support -= 4;
RG.district('hamburg', {loyalty: 6});
RG.district('bremen', {loyalty: 6});
Q.lean_ultraleft += 2;
!}

The General Workers' Union takes in tens of thousands of members in its first month.

@moscow
subtitle: [? if lock_moscow_orders = 1 : Against the party line: costs Unity. ?] The Zentrale goes back to the [? if e20_lux_in = 1 : Spartacists ?][? if e20_lux_in = 0 : Left ?], and the party stands in the election.
view-if: e20_lead_ul = 1
choose-if: lock_moscow_orders < 2
unavailable-subtitle: The [+ leading_faction_adj +] line forbids taking orders from Moscow.
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.lock_moscow_orders == 1) { Q.unity -= 10; Q[Q.leading_faction + '_satisfaction'] -= 10; }
Q.leading_faction = Q.e20_lux_in ? 'luxemburgist' : 'offensive';
Q.junior_faction = 'ultraleft';
Q.election_boycott = 0;
Q.ultraleft_satisfaction -= 20;
RG.ecci('lenin', 8);
!}

The Central Committee accepts Moscow's letter by a narrow vote, and the Left Radical leaders resign from the Zentrale.
